    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Steps:</b></p>
<ul>
	<li>Go to <a href="https://forkify.qa-academy.eu/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">forkify // Search over 1,000,000 recipes</a>.</li>
	<li>Click <b>Add Recipe</b>.Beef</li>
	<li>Enter valid data in all required fields.</li>
	<li>Enter <b>99999999999999999999999</b> in the <b>Prep Time</b> field.</li>
	<li>Enter <b>99999999999999999999999</b> in the <b>Servings</b> field.</li>
	<li>Enter valid ingredient data.</li>
	<li>Click the <b>UPLOAD</b> button.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Actual result</b> : Accepts excessively large numeric values and displays them in the recipe details as scientific notation (<b>1e+23 minutes</b> and <b>1e+24 servings</b>).</p>

<p><b>Expected Result</b> : Accept maximum of 4 ** digits in the <b>Prep Time</b> and <b>Servings</b> fields. If the limit is exceeded, it need to display an appropriate validation message and prevent the recipe from being uploaded.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

