    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Steps:</b></p>
<ul>
	<li>Go to <a href="https://forkify.qa-academy.eu/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">forkify // Search over 1,000,000 recipes</a>.</li>
	<li>Click <b>Add Recipe</b>.Beef</li>
	<li>Enter valid data in the <b>Title</b>, <b>URL</b>, <b>Image URL</b>, and <b>Publisher</b> fields.</li>
	<li>Enter valid values in the <b>Prep Time</b> and <b>Servings</b> fields.</li>
	<li>In <b>Ingredient</b> field 1, enter <b>full,half,boil</b></li>
	<li>Click the <b>Upload</b> button</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Actual result</b> : Accepts a non-numeric value in the ingredient quantity field and uploads the recipe successfully.But this non-numeric value was not displayed.</p>

<p><b>Expected Result</b> : Need to accept only numeric values in the ingredient quantity field, display an appropriate validation message for non-numeric input and prevent the recipe from being uploaded.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

