    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Steps:</b></p>
<ul>
	<li>Go to <a href="https://forkify.qa-academy.eu/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">forkify // Search over 1,000,000 recipes</a>.</li>
	<li>Click <b>Add Recipe</b>.Beef</li>
	<li>Enter valid data in the <b>Title</b>, <b>URL</b>, <b>Image URL</b>, and <b>Publisher</b> fields.</li>
	<li>Enter valid values in the <b>Prep Time</b> and <b>Servings</b> fields.</li>
	<li>In <b>Ingredient field 1</b>, enter any one of the following invalid formats:
	<ul>
		<li>1,,</li>
		<li>,g,</li>
		<li>,,Beef mince</li>
		<li>1,g,</li>
		<li>1,,Beef mince</li>
		<li>,g,Beef mince</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li>Click the <b>UPLOAD</b> button.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Actual result</b> : The application accepts missing ingredient values and uploads the recipe with showing successful validation message.</p>

<p><b>Expected Result</b> : Need to display an appropriate validation message for invalid ingredient missing data and prevent the recipe from being uploaded until all required ingredient values(Quantity , Unit , Description) are provided.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

