    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Steps</b> :</p>
<ul>
	<li>Go to <a href="https://forkify.qa-academy.eu/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">forkify // Search over 1,000,000 recipes</a></li>
	<li>Click <b>Add Recipe</b>.</li>
	<li>Enter fractional data in the <b>Title</b>, <b>URL</b>, <b>Image URL</b>, and <b>Publisher</b> fields.</li>
	<li>Enter 1 in the <b>Preparation Time</b> and <b>Servings</b> fields.</li>
	<li>Enter data <b>Ingredient field 1:</b> <tt>2,cup,Cooked rice</tt>.</li>
	<li>Enter data <b>Ingredient field 2:</b> <tt>200,g,Chicken breast</tt>.</li>
	<li>Enter data <b>Ingredient field 3:</b> <tt>100,ml,Heavy cream</tt>.</li>
	<li>Enter data <b>Ingredient field 4:</b> <tt>1,piece,Carrot (diced)</tt>.</li>
	<li>Enter data <b>Ingredient field 5:</b> <tt>1,tbsp,Butter</tt>.</li>
	<li>Enter data <b>Ingredient field 6:</b> <tt>1,pinch,Salt</tt>.</li>
	<li>Upload recipe.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Actual result</b> : <b>Title</b>, <b>URL</b>, <b>Image URL</b>, and <b>Publisher</b> fields accepts and saves fractional values successfully.</p>

<p><b>Expected Result</b> : The application need to display validation messages for invalid fields and prevent the recipe from being uploaded.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
