    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Steps</b> :</p>
<ul>
	<li>Go to <a href="https://forkify.qa-academy.eu/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">forkify // Search over 1,000,000 recipes</a></li>
	<li>Click <b>Add Recipe</b>.</li>
	<li>Enter only <b>spaces</b> in the <b>Title</b>, <b>URL</b>, <b>Image URL</b>, and <b>Publisher</b> fields.</li>
	<li>Enter <b>0</b> in the <b>Preparation Time</b> and <b>Servings</b> fields.</li>
	<li>Enter only <b>spaces/tabs</b> in all <b>Ingredient</b> fields.</li>
	<li>Click the <b>Upload</b> button.</li>
	<li>Verify that the validation message <b>"Wrong ingredient format! Please use the correct format <img class="emoticon" src="https://jira.a1qa.com/images/icons/emoticons/smile.png" height="16" width="16" align="absmiddle" alt="" border="0"/>"</b> is displayed.</li>
	<li>Click <b>Add Recipe</b>.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Actual result</b> : Stuck on the validation message <b>"Wrong ingredient format! Please use the correct format <img class="emoticon" src="https://jira.a1qa.com/images/icons/emoticons/smile.png" height="16" width="16" align="absmiddle" alt="" border="0"/>".</b>Can't add more recipe.</p>

<p><b>Expected Result</b> : Allow the user to upload the recipe successfully even if they uploaded a wrong ingredient format input previously. </p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

